            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0502" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/969.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-03-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 376.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegraphic instruction of the 7th instant and to my telegrams to the Department
                    of the 8th and 9th<anchor n="1" xml:id="d573-f1"/> instant, relative to the
                    mobilization of United States troops on the Texas border and the assurances of
                    President Taft to President Diaz that the mobilization has no ulterior purpose
                    as far as Mexico is concerned, I have the honor to inclose to the Department
                    herewith copy of my note to the foreign office, which I handed the minister for
                    foreign affairs personally immediately upon receipt of the Department’s
                    instructions, and copy in translation of the reply of the foreign office. The
                    text of both these notes was given out by the foreign office and is printed in
                    all of the morning’s papers. Despite this publicity, Americans and Mexicans and
                    most of my diplomatic colleagues unite in believing that the mobilization has
                    some other end in view than that of practice maneuvers.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred Morris
                    Dearing.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d573-a1.xml" xpointer="d573-a1"/>
